to \"the exact PR head\". Lines 10-11 instead name \"the exact candidate SHA\" as the full-gate authority. The path instructions require policy text to \"name what actually enforces today\". As written, this paragraph overstates what CI tests on prose-only PRs, and it describes a queue candidate that the contract retired.\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Proposed wording</summary>\n\n```diff\n-push (except the machine-written `cq-state` ledger branch); the retired `merge-queue-gate` template's workflow ran no tests. Affected-test\n+push (except the machine-written `cq-state` ledger branch and recognized\n+prose/Python-only PRs, which skip the TS gates per the contract below); the\n+retired `merge-queue-gate` template's workflow ran no tests. Affected-test\n ...\n-checks run only in CI; green required CI on the exact candidate SHA is the\n+checks run only in CI; green required CI on the exact PR head is the\n```\n</details>\n\nAs per path instructions: \"enforcement claims must name what actually enforces today.\" Based on learnings, `docs/focused-checks-contract.md` is the canonical gate contract.","id":"5a32c93a0922e821d81128d9580402023675d0827002b4db50ee7ec82b668b8f","intervals":[[6,11]],"path":"policy/templates/affected-tests.md","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Align the CI-scope claims with the focused-checks contract."}],"head":"38d4be5ab7839fc81c26e2cc92a18f502a626189","head_tree":"013c2fa4bf520f2358e9d1367a3d73c21ab4fb44","input_scope":[{"blob":"e9dd6deec8db5e897592f86773531d5aea977d60","intervals":[[43,43],[59,59],[70,71],[99,100]],"path":"policy/README.md"},{"blob":"13ccd56f45aaac97e4ed7af9f53443c9cb762240","intervals":[[6,12],[16,16],[30,32],[45,45],[112,112]],"path":"policy/templates/affected-tests.md"},{"blob":"f0c5c3605e745ed45a758e5c1d4e1c4b112c8562","intervals":[[45,45],[72,72],[78,79],[90,100]],"path":"policy/templates/instances.json"},{"blob":"dbdccabf9a35aa2577b54e0267c3cb54f48bbbc0","intervals":[[296,296],[343,343],[347,3